title: tag:query
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Customising the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Insert a tag filter in the simplified query and search

`tag:query <tag|negative_tag|mixed_tag> <tag>` asks which field of the tag model to search ([[Hierarchical tags]]) and a tag, completing over the paths of the existing ones (a tag under several parents is offered by each), then adds `#=<tag>` — the tag of that path, and those under it — to the simplified query of the metarecord list and runs the search; the focus stays where it was ([[Tag syntax in simplified queries]]). For `negative_tag` and `mixed_tag` the filter names the field: `negative_tag #=<tag>`, the records that deny the tag or one under it. A path the simplified language must quote (a space in it) is inserted as `#="<tag>"`, and the query zone then takes the focus and gives it up, since a command line cannot carry those quotes with `stay`. The keys are `# t`, `# n` and `# m` ([[Tagging from the GUI]]). Written in the shipped `commands.js`, where its questions and what it runs can be edited ([[User commands]]).
